From: Mingyu Lei <leimy@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:16:35 -0700
Subject: FSA: block hypervisor host-share roots and sensitive paths on Windows

On Windows guest VMs (Parallels, VMware, VirtualBox), hypervisor
shared-folder providers expose the host filesystem via UNC namespaces
(\\Mac, \\psf, \\vmware-host, \\.host, \\vboxsvr, \\vboxsrv) that do not
match drive-letter blocklist rules or MaybeIsLocalUNCPath().

Rather than blanket-blocking all children under these UNC servers (which
would break legitimate VM use cases where Desktop, Documents, Downloads,
or project shares map to hypervisor UNC paths), this CL:
- Treats hypervisor share roots (e.g. \\Mac\Home, \\Mac\AllFiles,
  \\vmware-host\Shared Folders\<share>, \\vboxsvr\<share>) and top-level
  user folders (Desktop, Documents, Downloads) as kDontBlockChildren,
  preventing sites from obtaining a directory grant to the entire host
  home or share root while allowing access to subdirectories and files.
- Blocks sensitive host subdirectories (.ssh, .gnupg, Library, .config,
  .cache, .dbus, Applications, AppData) and shell startup dotfiles
  (.zshenv, .zshrc, .bashrc, .bash_profile, .profile) under hypervisor
  share roots with kBlockAllChildren (while preserving macOS
  Library/CloudStorage, Library/Containers, and Library/Mobile Documents
  exceptions).
- Adds suffix blocklist rules for .ssh and .gnupg with
 `kBlockAllChildren`.

